    "dataProcessingProtocol": "LC-MS/MS analyses were performed on a Q Exactive HF-X (Thermo Fisher Scientific) equipped with an UltiMate 3000 RSLC nano system (Thermo Fisher Scientific). The samples were reconstituted in 0.1% formic acid, followed by centrifugation (16,000g for 10 min). The supernatants were pressure-loaded onto a 2 cm microcapillary precolumn packed with C18 (3 μm, 120 Å, SunChrom, Friedrichsdorf, Germany). The precolumn was connected to a 12 cm 150-μm-inner diameter microcapillary analytical column packed with C18 (1.9 μm, 120 Å, Dr. Maisch) and equipped with a homemade electrospray emitter tip. The spray voltage was set to 2.2 kV and the heated capillary temperature to 270 °C. The LC gradient consisted of 0 min, 7% B; 14 min, 10% B; 51 min, 20% B; 68 min, 30% B; 69-75 min, 95% B (A = water, 0.1% [v/v] formic acid; B = ACN, 0.1% [v/v] formic acid) at a flow rate of 600 nL/min. Higher-energy collisional dissociation HCD MS/MS spectra were recorded in the data-dependent mode using a Top 20 method. MS1 spectra were measured with a resolution of 70,000, an AGC target of 3e6, a maximum injection time of 20 ms, and a mass range from m/z 300 to 1400 and HCD MS/MS spectra with a resolution of 17,500, an AGC target of 1e6, a maximum injection time of 60 ms, a 1.6 m/z isolation window and a normalized collision energy of 30. The precursor-ion mass and fragmentation tolerance were 10 µL/L and 20 µL/L, respectively. Peptide m/z that triggered MS/MS scans were dynamically excluded from further MS/MS scans for 18 s. A specific tryptic was searched with a maximum of three missed cleavages allowed. Mass shifts of +15.9949 Da (methionine oxidation, M), +57.0214 Da (C2H3NO, carbamidomethylation, C), and +88.9935 Da (C2H3NOS, IAM-derivatized persulfide, C) were identified as persulfidation.",
