    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Purified recombinant proteins (20μg) were incubated with 100 μM of NaHS at room temperature for 1 h. Then, the protein samples were alkylated with 55 mM of iodoacetamide (IAM) in the dark at room temperature for 30 min. Next, alkylated proteins were resolved by sodium dodecyl sulfate-polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis (SDS-PAGE) gel and stained with Coomassie Brilliant Blue. The gel bands corresponding to the recombinant proteins were sliced, destained with 50 mM of NH4HCO3 in 50% (v/v) acetonitrile (ACN), and subjected to in-gel digestion. The resulting peptides were extracted, desalted, and evaporated to dryness prior to liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry (LC-MS/MS) analysis.",
